$$
g (f (x)) \equiv x.
$$

Therefore, our objective is to achieve the perfect complete cycle of data transforming by training two dual models $(f$ and $g)$ in a joint manner.

# 3.2.1 Algorithm Description

As illustrated in Figure 1, the framework is composed of two parts: Primal Cycle and Dual Cycle. Primal Cycle starts from semantic frames $x$ , (1) first transforms the semantic representation to sentences by the function $f$ , (2) then computes the loss by the given loss function $l_{1}$ , (3) predicts the semantic meaning from the generated sentences,

Algorithm 1 Joint dual learning algorithm   
1: Input: a mini-batch of $n$ data pairs $\{(x_i, y_i)\}_{i=1}^n$ , the function of the primal task $f$ , the function of the dual task $g$ , the loss function for the primal task $l_1(.)$ , the loss function for the dual task $l_2(.)$ , and the learning rates $\gamma_1, \gamma_2$ ;  
2: repeat  
3: Start from data $x$ , transform $x$ by function $f$ : $f(x_i; \theta_{x \to y})$ ;  
4: Compute the loss by $l_1(.)$ ;  
5: Transform the output of the primal task by function $g$ : $g(f(x_i; \theta_{x \to y}); \theta_{y \to x})$ ;  
6: Compute the loss by $l_2(.)$ ;  
7: Update model parameters:  
8: $\theta_{x \to y} \gets \theta_{x \to y} - \gamma_1 \nabla_{\theta_{x \to y}} (\sum_{i=1}^n [l_1(f(x_i; \theta_{x \to y})) + l_2(g(f(x_i; \theta_{x \to y}); \theta_{y \to x}))])$ ;  
9: $\theta_{y \to x} \gets \theta_{y \to x} - \gamma_2 \nabla_{\theta_{y \to x}} (\sum_{i=1}^n [l_2(g(f(x_i; \theta_{x \to y}); \theta_{y \to x}))])$ ;  
10: Start from data $y$ , transform $y$ by function $g$ : $g(y_i; \theta_{y \to x})$ ;  
11: Compute the loss by $l_2(.)$ ;  
12: Transform the output of the dual task by function $f$ : $f(g(y_i; \theta_{y \to x}); \theta_{x \to y})$ ;  
13: Compute the loss by $l_1(.)$ ;  
14: Update model parameters:  
15: $\theta_{y \to x} \gets \theta_{y \to x} - \gamma_2 \nabla_{\theta_{y \to x}} (\sum_{i=1}^n [l_2(g(y_i; \theta_{y \to x})) + l_1(f(g(y_i; \theta_{y \to x}); \theta_{x \to y}))])$ ;  
16: $\theta_{x \to y} \gets \theta_{x \to y} - \gamma_1 \nabla_{\theta_{x \to y}} (\sum_{i=1}^n [l_1(f(g(y_i; \theta_{y \to x}); \theta_{x \to y}))])$ ;  
17: until convergence

